  <entry>
    <id>https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/153.7.0esr/releasenotes/</id>
    <title type="html">Thunderbird 153.7.0esr</title>
    <author>
      <name>Thunderbird</name>
      <uri>https://www.thunderbird.net</uri>
    </author>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/153.7.0esr/releasenotes/"/>
    <updated>2026-11-10T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <published>2026-11-10T00:00:00+00:00</published>

    <content type="html"><![CDATA[
      

  
  

  
    

    
      
        
        

        
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Opening a window could cause Thunderbird to crash</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>MP4 attachments could be truncated when forwarding messages</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Exchange autodiscovery failed when redirected to another email address</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Legacy IMAP tag changes were not sent to the server and reverted after refresh</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>SMTP Kerberos authentication failed on Linux with STARTTLS</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p><a href="https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/known-vulnerabilities/thunderbird/#thunderbird153.7">Security fixes</a></p>
          
        </li>
      
    
    </ul>
  
  

<p>As always, you’re encouraged to <a href="https://connect.mozilla.org/t5/ideas/idb-p/ideas/label-name/thunderbird">tell us what you think</a>, <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/questions/new/thunderbird">ask for help</a>, or <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=Thunderbird">file a bug in Bugzilla</a></p>
<style> li p { display: inline; } </style>
      ]]>
    </content>
